# Texas_Instruments_ADS7042IDCUR — component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint, LCSC
# pinned in properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields).
#
# NEW PART (2026-07-26, middleweight capture) — SUBSTITUTED for the brief's named ADS8353.
# Full LCSC/JLC sourcing search (many queries, 2026-07-26): ADS8353, ADS7853, ADS7253 (the
# whole pin-compatible dual-simultaneous-SAR family, datasheet SBAS584B read in full) have
# NO LCSC catalog listing in ANY package (WQFN-16 or TSSOP-16) and 0 JLC parts-search
# results — confirmed by the total absence of any lcsc.com product page across a dozen
# search variants (contrast with TMC2160A-TA and AS5047P-ATSM, which surfaced LCSC pages
# immediately). ADI AD7367/AD7366 (also true dual-simultaneous SAR): found on LCSC
# (C398821) but OUT OF STOCK. TI ADS8688/ADS8684 (LCSC C527390, 911 in stock, $4.28): real
# stock, but datasheet section 8.4.1.2 confirms it samples ONE channel per CS edge through
# a SHARED SAR core (fast-multiplexed, not simultaneous) — does not meet the "simultaneous
# sampling" requirement, ruled out.
#
# RESOLUTION: two independent ADS7042 (LCSC C701641, ADS7042IDCUR, VSSOP-8, 2,922 in stock
# @ ~$2.10, checked 2026-07-26) with their CS pins tied to the SAME net (middleweight.zen).
# ADS7042 is a 12-bit, 1 MSPS, CS-edge-triggered, single-channel SAR ADC (datasheet
# SBAS608C read in full) — tying two chips' CS together starts both chips' track-and-hold +
# conversion on the identical clock edge, which is a true hardware-simultaneous-sample
# realization of the same principle ADS8353 uses internally (two independent SAR cores),
# just as two packages instead of one. Each chip gets its own SDO (separate PIO-SPI reads;
# the simultaneity is in the shared CS edge, not the readout). This is a DOWNGRADE from
# ADS8353's 16-bit to ADS7042's 12-bit — explicitly sanctioned by CLAUDE.md's own canonical
# table ("ADS8353/ADS7253-class dual simultaneous SAR") and by the brief's own "cheaper
# alt: ADS8354 (14-bit)" allowance. Resolution check: 200mV/A x ~5.6A peak = 1.12V FS into
# a 0-3.3V AVDD reference -> 12-bit LSB = 3.3V/4096 = 0.8mV = 4mA of current resolution —
# comfortably adequate for a NEMA23 FOC loop. FLAGGED for Ben (open item, see session
# report) — an alternate genuinely-stocked true-dual-SAR IC, if one turns up, would let this
# revert to a single-package solution.
#
# Datasheet SBAS608C findings: AVDD=DVDD=1.65-3.6V (single 3V3 rail covers both — no
# separate 5V needed); AINP/AINM single-ended (AINM tied to GND); "AVDD used as Reference
# for device" (ratiometric, 0-AVDD unipolar range, no external VREF); CS falling edge
# starts acquisition, SCLK reads out 12 bits, CS rising ends the frame (same 3-wire idiom
# as ADS8681/ADS8688's interface — familiar pattern). DCU package = 8-pin leaded VSSOP
# (matches the fetched footprint), not the X2QFN — the more hand/reflow-friendly choice.
DVDD = io("DVDD", Net, optional = True)
SCLK = io("SCLK", Net, optional = True)
SDO = io("SDO", Net, optional = True)
CS = io("CS", Net, optional = True)
AINM = io("AINM", Net, optional = True)
AINP = io("AINP", Net, optional = True)
AVDD = io("AVDD", Net, optional = True)
GND = io("GND", Net, optional = True)

Component(
    name = "Texas_Instruments_ADS7042IDCUR",
    footprint = File("Texas_Instruments_ADS7042IDCUR/VSSOP-8_L2.3-W2.0-P0.50-LS3.1-BR.kicad_mod"),
    symbol = Symbol("Texas_Instruments_ADS7042IDCUR/Texas_Instruments_ADS7042IDCUR.kicad_sym"),
    prefix = "U",
    part = Part(mpn = "ADS7042IDCUR", manufacturer = "Texas Instruments"),
    properties = {"LCSC": "C701641", "MPN": "ADS7042IDCUR"},
    pins = {
        "DVDD": DVDD,
        "SCLK": SCLK,
        "SDO": SDO,
        "~{CS}": CS,
        "AINM": AINM,
        "AINP": AINP,
        "AVDD": AVDD,
        "GND": GND,
    },
)
